body:
The function doc doesn't currently explain *why* widening is all-or-nothing rather than structural, which is the whole point of this fix (issue #1126: `[]T` is not assignable to `[]interface{}`, but is assignable to `interface{}`). Worth spelling out so a future reader doesn't "simplify" this back into a structural rewrite.

```suggestion
// replaceTypeParamsWithAny replaces type parameters with interface{} for use in
// non-generic contexts like HookContextImpl methods. Widening is all-or-nothing:
// composite types that merely mention a type parameter (e.g. []T, map[K]V) become
// a bare interface{}, not a structurally rewritten equivalent (e.g. []interface{}),
// since only the former is assignable from the concrete value the trampoline holds.
// Hook authors must type-assert accordingly.
```

