body:
@Harsh63870   I’d go with expanding `$root` during setup, since that keeps it consistent with positive targets and the documented syntax.

One case worth covering is `target: "**"` with `exclude_targets: ["$root"]`: root-module resolution should still happen when only the exclusion uses `$root`, with a clear error if no root module is found.

Could you add a setup-level test showing that the root package and its subpackages are excluded, while an unrelated dependency still matches? Doing the expansion before concurrent matching would also keep the shared rules read-only.
